LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Sensitivity"
English sensitivity analysis means testing how much an answer changes when an input changes, and the word carries no suggestion of delicacy or of feeling. The related phrase sensitive to is used of the answer, not of the analyst: an answer is sensitive to volume if volume moves it a great deal. Arabic حساسية carries the same two senses as English and the technical one has to be learned from context. French analyse de sensibilité is the settled term, and French usefully adds élasticité for the particular sensitivity of demand to price, which Chapter 11 computes — so in French the general idea and the specific measure have different names, where English uses sensitivity for both and elasticity only for the second.
